WEBVTT

1
00:58:23.786 --> 00:58:25.786
Have you met someone new?

2
00:58:27.786 --> 00:58:29.786
Is there anyone here for the first time this morning?

3
00:58:30.786 --> 00:58:31.786
Good morning.

4
00:58:33.786 --> 00:58:34.786
Where are you from?

5
00:58:36.786 --> 00:58:37.786
The Netherlands, okay, where?

6
00:58:39.786 --> 00:58:40.786
Eindhoven, hallelujah.

7
00:58:53.786 --> 00:58:54.786
Okay, welcome.

8
00:58:55.786 --> 00:58:56.786
Welcome.

9
00:58:58.786 --> 00:58:59.786
I pray that the Lord will bless you.

10
00:59:01.786 --> 00:59:02.786
Amen.

11
00:59:07.786 --> 00:59:09.786
We will continue with the worship by giving to the Lord.

12
00:59:16.786 --> 00:59:17.786
Hallelujah.

13
00:59:18.786 --> 00:59:19.786
Oh, God is so good.

14
00:59:19.786 --> 00:59:26.786
God always has slightly different ideas and slightly different plans than we humans do.

15
00:59:27.786 --> 00:59:40.786
And this week I really felt that, because He is so great and so good, it is so beautiful to bring something back to Him as thanks.

16
00:59:41.786 --> 00:59:47.786
And when I hear what we have already received this morning, it is so beautiful.

17
00:59:47.786 --> 00:59:51.786
There are many things that resonate with what I have received this week.

18
00:59:52.786 --> 00:59:56.786
God really wants, He really wants, He does not just want to do something casually.

19
00:59:57.786 --> 01:00:01.786
It is not nice to just say, oh, nice Sunday and we will just continue happily.

20
01:00:02.786 --> 01:00:13.786
And the text I have for today is really a piece of teaching that Paul has given us and that is also important for us at this moment.

21
01:00:13.786 --> 01:00:20.786
And I want to take you, yes, actually take you to a kind of thank offering with this from this morning.

22
01:00:21.786 --> 01:00:22.786
I don't know if the text is already there.

23
01:00:23.786 --> 01:00:24.786
Oh yes, it's already there.

24
01:00:25.786 --> 01:00:26.786
Then I'll just get started.

25
01:00:27.786 --> 01:00:30.786
And it says, but it has gone as it is written in the books.

26
01:00:31.786 --> 01:00:35.786
So Paul also knew the Bible as far as he was prepared at that time.

27
01:00:36.786 --> 01:00:39.786
And he talks about Isaiah 64 for anyone who feels like looking at it.

28
01:00:40.786 --> 01:00:41.786
That is really a challenge.

29
01:00:41.786 --> 01:00:45.786
And what does the Bible say there? No one has ever seen anything like it.

30
01:00:46.786 --> 01:00:48.786
No one has ever heard anything like it.

31
01:00:49.786 --> 01:00:51.786
No human has ever been able to conceive such things.

32
01:00:52.786 --> 01:00:56.786
But this is precisely the plan for the people who love him.

33
01:00:57.786 --> 01:01:02.786
This is, yes, you can only understand this if you know Jesus.

34
01:01:03.786 --> 01:01:07.786
And now God has revealed his plan to us through his spirit.

35
01:01:07.786 --> 01:01:10.786
For God's spirit knows everything.

36
01:01:11.786 --> 01:01:14.786
He also knows the deepest thoughts and plans of God.

37
01:01:15.786 --> 01:01:18.786
Who can know what lives deep in the thoughts of a person?

38
01:01:19.786 --> 01:01:20.786
That can only be his own spirit.

39
01:01:21.786 --> 01:01:25.786
And in the same way, only God's own spirit knows what is in God.

40
01:01:26.786 --> 01:01:31.786
And we have not received the spirit of this world, as we have already heard this morning.

41
01:01:32.786 --> 01:01:34.786
No, we have received the spirit of God.

42
01:01:34.786 --> 01:01:37.786
And because of that, we can know what God has given us.

43
01:01:39.786 --> 01:01:42.786
And this is written in various places in the Bible.

44
01:01:43.786 --> 01:01:47.786
In the prophets, the books leading to Jesus, it is also written in various places.

45
01:01:48.786 --> 01:01:53.786
In Habakkuk, in Isaiah, it is very clearly stated about God's higher plans that we often do not understand.

46
01:01:54.786 --> 01:01:56.786
And yet God wants us to understand it.

47
01:01:57.786 --> 01:01:59.786
That is a very deep desire of His.

48
01:02:00.786 --> 01:02:02.786
He wants us to understand Him.

49
01:02:02.786 --> 01:02:04.786
That we grasp what He feels.

50
01:02:05.786 --> 01:02:06.786
That we grasp what He thinks.

51
01:02:07.786 --> 01:02:12.786
And often we must first go through a kind of fiery trial of faith to better understand His plan.

52
01:02:13.786 --> 01:02:14.786
To better understand Him.

53
01:02:15.786 --> 01:02:18.786
And then it is up to us to receive, with a broken heart, what we have also seen this morning,

54
01:02:19.786 --> 01:02:21.786
a broken heart from Him.

55
01:02:23.786 --> 01:02:27.786
For what He has done, it is real, it breaks your heart.

56
01:02:28.786 --> 01:02:32.786
And one of those things from His plan that God has accomplished, which was once impossible,

57
01:02:33.786 --> 01:02:34.786
before Jesus came,

58
01:02:35.786 --> 01:02:39.786
and sometimes still seems impossible to us even after Jesus has come,

59
01:02:40.786 --> 01:02:46.786
is God's intention to use you and me to be His holy temple.

60
01:02:47.786 --> 01:02:49.786
His temple of the Holy Spirit.

61
01:02:50.786 --> 01:02:52.786
That is true, that is true, that is true.

62
01:02:53.786 --> 01:02:55.786
His temple of his Holy Spirit.

63
01:02:56.786 --> 01:02:57.786
That is really mindblowing.

64
01:02:58.786 --> 01:03:03.786
He needs your and my heart as a temple in which he can dwell

65
01:03:04.786 --> 01:03:08.786
and dedicate his examples to shape his kingdom.

66
01:03:09.786 --> 01:03:10.786
This is God's plan.

67
01:03:11.786 --> 01:03:16.786
He needs our hearts that are filled with worship, in prayer, in sowing and working through his Holy Spirit.

68
01:03:17.786 --> 01:03:20.786
And not just on Sunday or Monday, but simply every day.

69
01:03:21.786 --> 01:03:26.786
And in this way, he builds his kingdom, because he has chosen to do it this way.

70
01:03:27.786 --> 01:03:31.786
So his choice to do this was not necessary, but he chose to do so.

71
01:03:32.786 --> 01:03:33.786
You and me.

72
01:03:34.786 --> 01:03:36.786
And our sowing is also part of this.

73
01:03:37.786 --> 01:03:39.786
Sowing is a holy act of faith.

74
01:03:40.786 --> 01:03:42.786
A holy part of his temple service.

75
01:03:43.786 --> 01:03:48.786
And let us also sow this morning with this view of Jesus.

76
01:03:48.786 --> 01:03:50.786
To make God happy in this way.

77
01:03:51.786 --> 01:03:56.786
For only by reflecting on him and obeying in faith, can he be made happy.

78
01:03:57.786 --> 01:04:01.786
But let us not look to human logic and the often accompanying stubbornness or shortsightedness.

79
01:04:02.786 --> 01:04:06.786
God is truly much greater and much more beautiful and much better.

80
01:04:07.786 --> 01:04:12.786
Let us not chase the foolishness of this society, without the guidance of a good shepherd.

81
01:04:13.786 --> 01:04:16.786
But let us seek wisdom from God's own Spirit.

82
01:04:17.786 --> 01:04:22.786
For the so-called wise and understanding, the plans of the Father are safely hidden.

83
01:04:23.786 --> 01:04:27.786
But to us, His children, they have been revealed by His Holy Spirit.

84
01:04:30.786 --> 01:04:32.786
So let us look to Jesus.

85
01:04:33.786 --> 01:04:37.786
And perhaps it is nice to stand before Him again.

86
01:04:38.786 --> 01:04:44.786
And to take sowing seriously and to bring this as worship to Him.

87
01:04:45.786 --> 01:04:47.786
For Jesus, You are the true Lamb of God.

88
01:04:48.786 --> 01:04:50.786
You are the only one with the right to speak.

89
01:04:51.786 --> 01:04:53.786
You were silent at that moment.

90
01:04:54.786 --> 01:04:58.786
You were still and You died in complete obedience to the Father.

91
01:04:59.786 --> 01:05:03.786
And You went to the cross and on the cross, You drew all people to Yourself.

92
01:05:04.786 --> 01:05:11.786
Death could not hold You, because through the cross, You took away all authority, all power, all dominion from evil.

93
01:05:11.786 --> 01:05:14.786
And You are the only and true victor.

94
01:05:15.786 --> 01:05:17.786
Lord, You have saved us from evil with this.

95
01:05:20.786 --> 01:05:24.786
Lord, thank You for who You are and for what You have done and for all that You will do.

96
01:05:27.786 --> 01:05:31.786
Lord, it is up to us to receive from You through daily total surrender to You, Lord.

97
01:05:32.786 --> 01:05:42.786
And I also pray that this morning we may bring a total surrender to You and to Your ways, to Your plans, our gifts, Lord, as a thank offering for today.

98
01:05:43.786 --> 01:05:46.786
And so I bless us all in the name of King Jesus.

99
01:05:47.786 --> 01:05:49.786
Many blessings as we bring back today.

100
01:05:51.786 --> 01:05:52.786
Amen.

101
01:05:53.786 --> 01:05:56.786
I want to exist, please stand still for just a moment, because I would really like to pray for us.

102
01:05:57.786 --> 01:05:58.786
Then you may sit down.

103
01:06:01.786 --> 01:06:05.786
As you know, we are now in the Open Relationships Month.

104
01:06:06.786 --> 01:06:10.786
And I sent an email at the beginning of this, or somewhere this week.

105
01:06:11.786 --> 01:06:16.786
And in that email, I wrote that today we are going to talk about grief, the subject of grief.

106
01:06:17.786 --> 01:06:28.786
And this concerns not only those who have dealt with the loss of a loved one in their own lives, but it concerns the whole congregation.

107
01:06:29.786 --> 01:06:34.786
For we all have a relationship with someone who has experienced that.

108
01:06:35.786 --> 01:06:45.786
So whether you have to learn to deal with this intense pain in life yourself, or whether you know someone, it concerns the whole body of Christ.

109
01:06:46.786 --> 01:06:51.786
So I would appreciate it if we could close our eyes so that I can bless us before we go into the Word.

110
01:06:52.786 --> 01:06:55.786
Father in heaven, I thank you for this day.

111
01:06:56.786 --> 01:06:57.786
Lord, I thank you for this Sunday.

112
01:06:58.786 --> 01:07:14.786
Lord, I pray that this Sunday will form a new step towards Jesus, towards healing, towards acceptance that there is a hopeful future for everyone who believes in Jesus.

113
01:07:14.786 --> 01:07:26.786
Father, I want to pray in the name of Jesus that when there are people in the room who are dealing with intense pain and even disappointment or even defensiveness.

114
01:07:27.786 --> 01:07:34.786
Lord, I pray Holy Spirit that you take the lead in all the hearts of the people at this moment.

115
01:07:34.786 --> 01:07:39.786
Also for those people who say it doesn't have to be for me anymore, too much pain.

116
01:07:40.786 --> 01:07:44.786
Lord, I want to pray that you will knock on the door again.

117
01:07:45.786 --> 01:07:48.786
Jesus says I stand at the door and knock.

118
01:07:49.786 --> 01:07:50.786
Open up.

119
01:07:51.786 --> 01:07:53.786
Then I can come in and have a meal with you.

120
01:07:54.786 --> 01:07:59.786
In other words, then He can be in our fellowship and intimacy with us.

121
01:07:59.786 --> 01:08:07.786
And so I bless Open Church in Jesus' name that today may be a day of new insight, enlightenment.

122
01:08:08.786 --> 01:08:14.786
Both in the symbolic form but also literally that Jesus may shine his light in our hearts.

123
01:08:15.786 --> 01:08:16.786
In Jesus' name. Amen.

124
01:08:17.786 --> 01:08:18.786
Amen. Please have a seat.

125
01:08:19.786 --> 01:08:20.786
Ben, thank you all very much.

126
01:08:20.786 --> 01:08:21.786
Ben, thank you all very much.

127
01:08:27.786 --> 01:08:28.786
Have a nice day.

128
01:08:29.786 --> 01:08:30.786
Very good. Nice.

129
01:08:31.786 --> 01:08:32.786
Alright.

130
01:08:35.786 --> 01:08:43.786
It was Bram's idea to discuss this topic.

131
01:08:44.786 --> 01:08:52.786
And first of all, wonderful Bram, I want to thank you for making yourself available to share this.

132
01:08:53.786 --> 01:09:03.786
Church, I want to ask all of us, and I know we are going to do this, but that we truly respect everything you hear today.

133
01:09:04.786 --> 01:09:10.786
You are going to hear an experience that a good 80% of this church does not know.

134
01:09:11.786 --> 01:09:15.786
About Bram, our elder, and Els. Els is at home at this moment, I think.

135
01:09:18.786 --> 01:09:23.786
Bram's story serves as a guide for your story.

136
01:09:24.786 --> 01:09:25.786
Bram's story is Bram's story.

137
01:09:26.786 --> 01:09:27.786
And your story is your story.

138
01:09:28.786 --> 01:09:42.786
And so, we are not looking for instructions here on stage that if you have to learn to deal with grief, we say, you have grief, and these are the strategies on how to deal with it.

139
01:09:43.786 --> 01:09:44.786
That is not our intention.

140
01:09:45.786 --> 01:09:48.786
Our intention is a conversation, to share experiences.

141
01:09:49.786 --> 01:10:00.786
And the Bible does say that elders in the Bible are people who have experience and can teach.

142
01:10:01.786 --> 01:10:09.786
And that they have gone through tests and therefore have a degree of credibility to share their lives.

143
01:10:10.786 --> 01:10:25.786
And then it is, I don't know if you know the concept lead by example, but lead by example means in Dutch that Bram's life may lead in our lives by listening to how he went through things.

144
01:10:26.786 --> 01:10:29.786
So that we can learn from it and say okay, this is what I want to learn from.

145
01:10:30.786 --> 01:10:34.786
So Bram is not going to give instructions, but Bram is going to share about his life.

146
01:10:35.786 --> 01:10:36.786
Amen?

147
01:10:37.786 --> 01:10:44.786
So we are going to talk about grief, about specific grief, about losing a loved one.

148
01:10:45.786 --> 01:10:47.786
Grief can mean more.

149
01:10:48.786 --> 01:10:52.786
Grief can also mean that you are dealing with divorce, which for example causes a lot of pain.

150
01:10:53.786 --> 01:10:57.786
And that you end up sitting alone and say to yourself, I didn't want this.

151
01:10:58.786 --> 01:11:00.786
And that you have to deal with that, that is also grief.

152
01:11:01.786 --> 01:11:04.786
You have different forms of loss, of course.

153
01:11:05.786 --> 01:11:15.786
I want to focus specifically today, even though if you are dealing with loss on other topics, you can also learn from this.

154
01:11:16.786 --> 01:11:18.786
Only today we are specifically talking about the loss of a loved one.

155
01:11:19.786 --> 01:11:29.786
So the fact that we are having this conversation Bram, makes it clear that you unfortunately have experiences here.

156
01:11:30.786 --> 01:11:35.786
So you could start with the introduction of the story of what happened.

157
01:11:36.786 --> 01:11:43.786
Yes, I think it is good to just outline how our family was at that time.

158
01:11:45.786 --> 01:11:53.786
It was the mid-eighties, I don't think it was long ago, because some memories are really like yesterday.

159
01:11:54.786 --> 01:11:58.786
Els and I were in our mid-twenties.

160
01:11:59.786 --> 01:12:06.786
A few years earlier, we had bought a nice row house.

161
01:12:07.786 --> 01:12:11.786
And our first daughter, Rachel, was 2.5 years old.

162
01:12:12.786 --> 01:12:16.786
And we were expecting again.

163
01:12:17.786 --> 01:12:19.786
Very happy about it, wonderful.

164
01:12:19.786 --> 01:12:23.786
We were really in the building phase of life, in the building phase of the family.

165
01:12:24.786 --> 01:12:29.786
And we looked forward to enriching the family with another little daughter.

166
01:12:30.786 --> 01:12:32.786
It turned out to be a little daughter, which we didn't know at the time, by the way.

167
01:12:38.786 --> 01:12:40.786
And that was our Kirsten.

168
01:12:42.786 --> 01:12:48.786
And the first thing we saw of Kirsten, usually you see a few tufts of hair on top of the head.

169
01:12:49.786 --> 01:12:52.786
The first thing we saw of Kirsten were two little feet.

170
01:12:53.786 --> 01:13:02.786
Two little feet, with ten toes, that started to squirm a bit, wondering what is this, what am I feeling now.

171
01:13:03.786 --> 01:13:05.786
And that is how Kirsten was born.

172
01:13:05.786 --> 01:13:19.786
After that, it quickly became clear that something was not right.

173
01:13:20.786 --> 01:13:24.786
And it took a long time before it was clear what that was.

174
01:13:25.786 --> 01:13:27.786
That is a difficult period.

175
01:13:28.786 --> 01:13:33.786
She quickly ended up in the incubator and it was clear that she had a problem with her heart.

176
01:13:34.786 --> 01:13:38.786
Because she was having trouble getting enough oxygen.

177
01:13:39.786 --> 01:13:42.786
And that has to do with heart circulation and so on.

178
01:13:44.786 --> 01:13:48.786
And then, it was also clear that something more was going on.

179
01:13:49.786 --> 01:13:54.786
But only after about a week and a half, it became clear that she also had Down syndrome.

180
01:13:55.786 --> 01:14:08.786
Then you have, you know, sometimes the uncertainty is worse than the situation at hand.

181
01:14:09.786 --> 01:14:11.786
And those ten days felt like an eternity.

182
01:14:12.786 --> 01:14:14.786
And then you also have doctors who start speculating.

183
01:14:15.786 --> 01:14:17.786
You really don't gain anything from that, I can tell you.

184
01:14:18.786 --> 01:14:20.786
Yes, we think about this, yes we think about that.

185
01:14:21.786 --> 01:14:22.786
Okay.

186
01:14:28.786 --> 01:14:34.786
For us, the attitude was immediately, wait a minute.

187
01:14:36.786 --> 01:14:39.786
In the uncertainty, in the not knowing.

188
01:14:40.786 --> 01:14:44.786
We did have an immediate foundational attitude, this is our little girl.

189
01:14:45.786 --> 01:14:53.786
Also she, we will take care of her, we will help her as much as we can.

190
01:14:54.786 --> 01:14:58.786
That has been an automatic reaction.

191
01:15:00.786 --> 01:15:03.786
You know, that has to do with how you look at children.

192
01:15:04.786 --> 01:15:06.786
Children are not our property.

193
01:15:07.786 --> 01:15:09.786
Children are entrusted to us.

194
01:15:10.786 --> 01:15:18.786
And it is our task as parents to be the best parents we can be.

195
01:15:19.786 --> 01:15:22.786
And to raise children.

196
01:15:23.786 --> 01:15:26.786
That is an active thing, it doesn't happen by itself, you have to work at it.

197
01:15:27.786 --> 01:15:32.786
To help children move forward, in various ways.

198
01:15:33.786 --> 01:15:34.786
Yes.

199
01:15:35.786 --> 01:15:39.786
So that was the beginning of the story, I'm just trying to find the thread.

200
01:15:40.786 --> 01:15:43.786
From time to time I will lose it, that is also the reason I asked,

201
01:15:44.786 --> 01:15:47.786
please do an interview for him Tim, because then you help me.

202
01:15:48.786 --> 01:15:51.786
Yes, I am used to having to sit here.

203
01:15:52.786 --> 01:15:59.786
So you find out, in principle, Kirsten was not born in the normal way.

204
01:15:59.786 --> 01:16:00.786
It was a convulsive birth.

205
01:16:01.786 --> 01:16:02.786
It was a convulsive birth.

206
01:16:03.786 --> 01:16:06.786
And then eventually you find out that she has a heart defect.

207
01:16:07.786 --> 01:16:08.786
That had nothing to do with it, of course.

208
01:16:09.786 --> 01:16:10.786
No.

209
01:16:11.786 --> 01:16:13.786
And you find out that she suffers from death.

210
01:16:14.786 --> 01:16:15.786
Yes.

211
01:16:16.786 --> 01:16:25.786
And what is your first reaction that you go through when you realize that it is not as it should be?

212
01:16:26.786 --> 01:16:31.786
That was not the biggest, the most difficult thing we had to deal with was the uncertainty.

213
01:16:32.786 --> 01:16:34.786
That was really very difficult.

214
01:16:36.786 --> 01:16:45.786
And after it became clearer what was going on, you can also determine your own position and we said to each other, well we will do our best.

215
01:16:46.786 --> 01:16:47.786
Were you religious at that time?

216
01:16:48.786 --> 01:16:49.786
Yes, absolutely.

217
01:16:49.786 --> 01:16:52.786
We both came to repentance at the age of about eighteen.

218
01:16:53.786 --> 01:16:55.786
We were also in this church at that time.

219
01:16:56.786 --> 01:17:03.786
So also the realization, as I just said, it is not you get a child, no you get to take care of a child.

220
01:17:04.786 --> 01:17:06.786
So we both had that realization.

221
01:17:07.786 --> 01:17:08.786
Yes.

222
01:17:09.786 --> 01:17:10.786
Yes, as a piece of basic understanding.

223
01:17:11.786 --> 01:17:12.786
Yes.

224
01:17:12.786 --> 01:17:21.786
So Kirsten had a disability and to be honest, Down syndrome played very little role at the beginning.

225
01:17:22.786 --> 01:17:28.786
Because yes, let's be honest, it is also a young baby.

226
01:17:29.786 --> 01:17:30.786
A baby that was developing.

227
01:17:31.786 --> 01:17:32.786
Yes.

228
01:17:32.786 --> 01:17:39.786
And one of the things that is so essential is, God has created every person.

229
01:17:40.786 --> 01:17:42.786
God has created every person in their own unique way.

230
01:17:43.786 --> 01:17:47.786
I don't know what happened for Down syndrome to develop.

231
01:17:48.786 --> 01:17:51.786
But I do know that it is a very important part.

232
01:17:52.786 --> 01:17:53.786
Yes.

233
01:17:54.786 --> 01:17:56.786
That it is a very important part.

234
01:17:56.786 --> 01:18:00.786
I don't know what happened for Down syndrome to develop.

235
01:18:01.786 --> 01:18:06.786
But I do know that it is a unique little person, a unique human being loved and wanted by God.

236
01:18:07.786 --> 01:18:08.786
Yes.

237
01:18:08.786 --> 01:18:09.786
And also wanted by us.

238
01:18:09.786 --> 01:18:10.786
Yes.

239
01:18:11.786 --> 01:18:13.786
The heart defect did have a lot of consequences.

240
01:18:15.786 --> 01:18:21.786
That led to Kirsten spending long, considerable periods in the hospital.

241
01:18:22.786 --> 01:18:24.786
She was born on November 19, 1988.

242
01:18:24.786 --> 01:18:26.786
She was home for Christmas.

243
01:18:27.786 --> 01:18:29.786
That was a big step at the time.

244
01:18:30.786 --> 01:18:33.786
It was the first time a child came home without nutrition.

245
01:18:34.786 --> 01:18:37.786
She had a tube through her nose for nutrition because she didn't have the energy.

246
01:18:38.786 --> 01:18:41.786
With a heart defect, you lack energy, you lack strength.

247
01:18:42.786 --> 01:18:44.786
That money is also for her as a baby.

248
01:18:45.786 --> 01:18:48.786
So she simply didn't have the energy to drink by herself.

249
01:18:49.786 --> 01:18:50.786
And she received it without nutrition.

250
01:18:50.786 --> 01:18:54.786
We were the first to take a baby home from the hospital.

251
01:18:55.786 --> 01:18:57.786
Who then received nutrition at home from the parents without it.

252
01:18:59.786 --> 01:19:01.786
That was quite something for the hospital.

253
01:19:02.786 --> 01:19:03.786
We really wanted that.

254
01:19:04.786 --> 01:19:07.786
Because at one point we said, listen, if she needs to be in the hospital, that's fine.

255
01:19:08.786 --> 01:19:10.786
If that extra care is needed, great that it's there.

256
01:19:11.786 --> 01:19:16.786
But if the only reason she is in the hospital is because she is receiving nutrition without it.

257
01:19:17.786 --> 01:19:18.786
We can arrange that at home too.

258
01:19:18.786 --> 01:19:20.786
Can you explain that nutrition?

259
01:19:21.786 --> 01:19:26.786
That is a tube that runs through the nose into the stomach.

260
01:19:27.786 --> 01:19:29.786
And then you give nutrition through that tube.

261
01:19:30.786 --> 01:19:32.786
Then Kirsten didn't have to do anything about it herself.

262
01:19:33.786 --> 01:19:34.786
She was simply given the nutrition.

263
01:19:39.786 --> 01:19:40.786
So that was how Kirsten was at home.

264
01:19:41.786 --> 01:19:45.786
She also spent periods of weeks in the hospital and then back home again.

265
01:19:46.786 --> 01:19:49.786
Had all sorts of complicated medical issues.

266
01:19:51.786 --> 01:19:56.786
For us, that meant an extremely intensive period.

267
01:19:58.786 --> 01:20:01.786
If someone who is busy says, I will never believe you again.

268
01:20:02.786 --> 01:20:03.786
Really.

269
01:20:04.786 --> 01:20:07.786
We were busy from 7 in the morning until 11 at night.

270
01:20:08.786 --> 01:20:09.786
We had 40 hours of family help.

271
01:20:10.786 --> 01:20:11.786
That was not enough.

272
01:20:11.786 --> 01:20:16.786
It happened that there was still ironing being done at 10 o'clock in the evening.

273
01:20:20.786 --> 01:20:23.786
She needed nutrition eight times a day.

274
01:20:24.786 --> 01:20:25.786
Later seven times.

275
01:20:26.786 --> 01:20:27.786
It could take up to an hour and a half each time.

276
01:20:28.786 --> 01:20:31.786
Because she couldn't tolerate too much at once.

277
01:20:32.786 --> 01:20:33.786
Then it all came out again.

278
01:20:34.786 --> 01:20:35.786
And you get nothing out of that. Nutrition has to stay in.

279
01:20:36.786 --> 01:20:44.786
It was often the case that the person who did the late feeding at 11 o'clock sometimes only went to bed at half past 12.

280
01:20:45.786 --> 01:20:49.786
We had agreed, whoever goes to bed late, can stay asleep.

281
01:20:50.786 --> 01:20:54.786
And the other one goes out at night if necessary.

282
01:20:55.786 --> 01:20:57.786
And that was two, three times a night.

283
01:20:58.786 --> 01:20:59.786
Very often that was necessary.

284
01:21:01.786 --> 01:21:03.786
This is how we lived for half a year.

285
01:21:04.786 --> 01:21:05.786
Yes, half a year.

286
01:21:08.786 --> 01:21:14.786
So, unfortunately, we are heading towards, how long did Kirsten ultimately live?

287
01:21:15.786 --> 01:21:16.786
Kirsten lived for eight months.

288
01:21:18.786 --> 01:21:19.786
In July she was in the hospital.

289
01:21:27.786 --> 01:21:28.786
You know that at some point.

290
01:21:29.786 --> 01:21:31.786
You get emotion, at the moment you least expect it.

291
01:21:31.786 --> 01:21:33.786
And this might be a moment you expect.

292
01:21:34.786 --> 01:21:35.786
On a Sunday morning she passed away.

293
01:21:36.786 --> 01:21:37.786
On a Sunday morning.

294
01:21:49.786 --> 01:21:51.786
Was it expected or was it unexpected?

295
01:21:52.786 --> 01:21:56.786
It was actually, good question.

296
01:21:57.786 --> 01:22:05.786
It was clear that she had serious problems.

297
01:22:06.786 --> 01:22:10.786
She was on the list for an open-heart surgery.

298
01:22:11.786 --> 01:22:19.786
And the perspective we had was that if that heart problem was resolved through surgical intervention,

299
01:22:20.786 --> 01:22:25.786
then she could lead a relatively normal life physically.

300
01:22:26.786 --> 01:22:28.786
Of course, still with Down syndrome.

301
01:22:29.786 --> 01:22:30.786
Which also has its limitations.

302
01:22:31.786 --> 01:22:35.786
But then you are talking about participating normally in a class.

303
01:22:36.786 --> 01:22:39.786
Perhaps an adapted class, maybe not.

304
01:22:40.786 --> 01:22:41.786
Those are the things you do not know.

305
01:22:42.786 --> 01:22:45.786
About just participating in sports activities.

306
01:22:46.786 --> 01:22:47.786
No, not a top athlete.

307
01:22:48.786 --> 01:22:49.786
Okay then, not a top athlete.

308
01:22:50.786 --> 01:22:51.786
You know.

309
01:22:52.786 --> 01:22:54.786
So that is what we envisioned as a future perspective for ourselves.

310
01:22:55.786 --> 01:22:58.786
A girl who would need some extra care and guidance.

311
01:22:59.786 --> 01:23:02.786
But where you do see a beautiful future.

312
01:23:03.786 --> 01:23:05.786
So you really had a vision for the future for Kirsten.

313
01:23:06.786 --> 01:23:07.786
Yes, for sure.

314
01:23:08.786 --> 01:23:17.786
And the passing was really unexpected.

315
01:23:18.786 --> 01:23:19.786
Really unexpected.

316
01:23:19.786 --> 01:23:21.786
In hindsight, her heart just gave up.

317
01:23:22.786 --> 01:23:26.786
And it did not make it to the operation in time.

318
01:23:29.786 --> 01:23:30.786
Okay.

319
01:23:31.786 --> 01:23:32.786
So.

320
01:23:35.786 --> 01:23:38.786
I am going to ask a question that is extremely cruel.

321
01:23:40.786 --> 01:23:43.786
And we have agreed that we will go through this together.

322
01:23:44.786 --> 01:23:48.786
But are you dealing with a child who has Down syndrome.

323
01:23:49.786 --> 01:23:51.786
And has a heart defect.

324
01:23:52.786 --> 01:23:54.786
And then it dies.

325
01:23:55.786 --> 01:23:57.786
Then you can say from a human perspective.

326
01:23:58.786 --> 01:24:01.786
Then there is now rest, because now the problem is solved.

327
01:24:02.786 --> 01:24:05.786
These are the reactions of people you have experienced.

328
01:24:06.786 --> 01:24:07.786
Can you tell us something about that?

329
01:24:08.786 --> 01:24:09.786
Yes, you know.

330
01:24:10.786 --> 01:24:12.786
Shall we leave that for a moment?

331
01:24:13.786 --> 01:24:14.786
Yes, that's fine.

332
01:24:19.786 --> 01:24:23.786
I cannot describe what happened up to the funeral.

333
01:24:24.786 --> 01:24:25.786
That is not possible.

334
01:24:27.786 --> 01:24:36.786
What happened afterwards was a powerlessness.

335
01:24:37.786 --> 01:24:39.786
A bewilderment.

336
01:24:40.786 --> 01:24:41.786
Yes.

337
01:24:41.786 --> 01:24:42.786
An emptiness.

338
01:24:43.786 --> 01:24:45.786
I searched for words.

339
01:24:46.786 --> 01:24:47.786
A loss.

340
01:24:48.786 --> 01:24:49.786
A pain.

341
01:24:50.786 --> 01:24:54.786
It was so unimaginably empty.

342
01:24:55.786 --> 01:24:57.786
You don't want to know that.

343
01:24:58.786 --> 01:25:00.786
You can't imagine that.

344
01:25:04.786 --> 01:25:07.786
But do you experience that during that time?

345
01:25:08.786 --> 01:25:14.786
For what we are looking for in this conversation are handles.

346
01:25:15.786 --> 01:25:22.786
Where people like yourself, Els, and the people in the body of Christ.

347
01:25:23.786 --> 01:25:28.786
That you try to find handles in the list of things you just wrote down.

348
01:25:29.786 --> 01:25:34.786
Powerlessness, bewilderment, emptiness, loss, sorrow, pain.

349
01:25:34.786 --> 01:25:36.786
I will read them out loud again.

350
01:25:37.786 --> 01:25:39.786
Then you can listen to the key words that Bram writes down.

351
01:25:40.786 --> 01:25:48.786
Powerlessness, bewilderment, emptiness, loss, sorrow, pain.

352
01:25:49.786 --> 01:25:59.786
A word I want to search for is anger, rage, defense, disappointment.

353
01:26:00.786 --> 01:26:03.786
So I have written down a question here.

354
01:26:04.786 --> 01:26:09.786
Bram, how do you deal with sorrow and anger?

355
01:26:10.786 --> 01:26:14.786
For the list was completely focused on sorrow.

356
01:26:15.786 --> 01:26:16.786
But how do you deal with anger in this?

357
01:26:17.786 --> 01:26:18.786
I have not experienced anger.

358
01:26:26.786 --> 01:26:27.786
And that is very personal.

359
01:26:27.786 --> 01:26:28.786
I know that other people do experience that.

360
01:26:29.786 --> 01:26:30.786
And I can understand it well.

361
01:26:49.786 --> 01:26:54.786
You know people, people immediately think, how can God do this?

362
01:26:55.786 --> 01:26:57.786
I don't know God like that.

363
01:26:58.786 --> 01:27:08.786
I don't see God, and I didn't see Him then, as a puppeteer who controls and leads everything on this earth precisely.

364
01:27:09.786 --> 01:27:19.786
And you know, if that were the case, then we would not have been created with a free will and the ability to choose.

365
01:27:19.786 --> 01:27:24.786
And with the ability to want to follow God out of love.

366
01:27:26.786 --> 01:27:31.786
And I know God as a good shepherd.

367
01:27:32.786 --> 01:27:38.786
I know God as the one who cares for us.

368
01:27:40.786 --> 01:27:42.786
This earth is broken.

369
01:27:42.786 --> 01:27:44.786
This earth is broken.

370
01:27:45.786 --> 01:27:53.786
In this world, it is a fallen world, those are the words, but it has just gone wrong here.

371
01:27:55.786 --> 01:27:56.786
And that hurts.

372
01:27:58.786 --> 01:28:10.786
But in everything, you know, when Jesus says that He is the good shepherd, then He is also the good shepherd when there is a sheep lying with a broken leg because a rock has fallen on it.

373
01:28:11.786 --> 01:28:13.786
At that moment, God is also a good shepherd.

374
01:28:13.786 --> 01:28:15.786
But that sheep is in pain.

375
01:28:16.786 --> 01:28:24.786
And so, I can only say, with all the powerlessness to express it.

376
01:28:24.786 --> 01:28:28.786
I mean, I can find words now, but I couldn't then.

377
01:28:30.786 --> 01:28:36.786
But the only thing you can really do is, go to God.

378
01:28:37.786 --> 01:28:40.786
And that is my, I am convinced, that has been my salvation.

379
01:28:44.786 --> 01:28:53.786
Even if you don't know how to say it, if you don't know how to express it, if you don't know what is going on, if you don't understand your own reaction and that of other people.

380
01:28:53.786 --> 01:28:56.786
I can't make heads or tails of it anymore.

381
01:28:57.786 --> 01:28:58.786
Then throw that down before God.

382
01:28:58.786 --> 01:29:00.786
If you are angry, throw your anger down before God.

383
01:29:02.786 --> 01:29:03.786
Whatever it may be.

384
01:29:03.786 --> 01:29:15.786
We just sang a song, and one of the lyrics, one of the lines in the song is remember that our God has never failed us.

385
01:29:19.786 --> 01:29:24.786
Can you sing that, in light of this situation?

386
01:29:24.786 --> 01:29:27.786
Now I can, but there are moments when I might not have been able to see that.

387
01:29:28.786 --> 01:29:44.786
And I can well imagine that, because every time I sing this song, without having experienced the loss of a loved one in my life, I can well imagine that we sing this as a church and at least half of us often has questions about it.

388
01:29:44.786 --> 01:29:47.786
Remember that our God has never failed us.

389
01:29:48.786 --> 01:29:52.786
Because you have of course prayed for Kirsten's healing.

390
01:29:53.786 --> 01:29:54.786
Yes.

391
01:29:55.786 --> 01:30:02.786
And how do you deal with that, this is unprepared, but how do you deal with it when you don't get what you have prayed for?

392
01:30:05.786 --> 01:30:06.786
Because that is a very important...

393
01:30:06.786 --> 01:30:10.786
You know, I don't know if you can say, you deal with that thing.

394
01:30:10.786 --> 01:30:23.786
You pray, you lay your matters before God, but in the meantime, you live your life and go to the wisdom and knowledge you have, you make your decisions and follow your life.

395
01:30:23.786 --> 01:30:24.786
Yes.

396
01:30:24.786 --> 01:30:33.786
And actually, who are we that we would call God to account?

397
01:30:34.786 --> 01:30:41.786
When Job did that, he received an answer from God, Job, Job, wait a minute, come here for a moment.

398
01:30:41.786 --> 01:30:44.786
Just one on one, we have something to discuss, just one on one.

399
01:30:44.786 --> 01:30:52.786
Look up, look at the heavens, who made that, look at the animals, who made that, look at...

400
01:30:53.786 --> 01:30:55.786
And then Job became very small.

401
01:30:56.786 --> 01:30:57.786
Yes.

402
01:30:57.786 --> 01:30:58.786
And...

403
01:31:02.786 --> 01:31:04.786
Ultimately, it comes down to...

404
01:31:05.786 --> 01:31:07.786
Ultimately, it is about relationship.

405
01:31:08.786 --> 01:31:14.786
Ultimately, when I spoke about this with our Rachel a few weeks ago.

406
01:31:14.786 --> 01:31:16.786
Rachel, give a wave.

407
01:31:16.786 --> 01:31:21.786
For those who don't know that Rachel is Bram's daughter, Rachel is Bram's daughter.

408
01:31:22.786 --> 01:31:26.786
Sometimes you are also amazed by the wisdom of your own children, you know.

409
01:31:28.786 --> 01:31:37.786
Then she said, the question is, who is God for you in that situation?

410
01:31:37.786 --> 01:31:38.786
Yes.

411
01:31:39.786 --> 01:31:42.786
Does God have anything to say to you in that situation?

412
01:31:43.786 --> 01:31:45.786
And I can't just say that...

413
01:31:45.786 --> 01:31:55.786
It was a disaster and I was in the middle of the unimaginable cloud of emotion that you cannot put into words.

414
01:31:55.786 --> 01:31:57.786
And then God spoke this and that.

415
01:31:58.786 --> 01:32:00.786
But seek the heart of God.

416
01:32:00.786 --> 01:32:04.786
Or at the very least, lay everything out before Him.

417
01:32:04.786 --> 01:32:06.786
And then it is about relationship.

418
01:32:06.786 --> 01:32:07.786
Yes.

419
01:32:07.786 --> 01:32:08.786
And that is the crux.

420
01:32:09.786 --> 01:32:16.786
I appreciate that you said that you yourself have not dealt with anger.

421
01:32:16.786 --> 01:32:18.786
But that you can understand it well.

422
01:32:20.786 --> 01:32:29.786
Do you have any advice or a comment for people who are dealing with anger?

423
01:32:30.786 --> 01:32:34.786
Just being literally angry at God.

424
01:32:34.786 --> 01:32:38.786
And literally holding it against Him that this has happened.

425
01:32:38.786 --> 01:32:39.786
And I can understand that well.

426
01:32:39.786 --> 01:32:41.786
I can imagine that well.

427
01:32:42.786 --> 01:32:46.786
I think there is only one place you should go with it, and that is to God Himself.

428
01:32:46.786 --> 01:32:48.786
The worst thing you can...

429
01:32:48.786 --> 01:32:51.786
Yes, well, the worst, the good, the best.

430
01:32:53.786 --> 01:32:57.786
Withdrawing and isolating is extremely harmful.

431
01:32:59.786 --> 01:33:02.786
And that is also a reaction you could understand.

432
01:33:02.786 --> 01:33:05.786
100,000 reactions we can all understand together.

433
01:33:05.786 --> 01:33:07.786
But not everything is good.

434
01:33:07.786 --> 01:33:10.786
If you want to be angry, then be angry at God.

435
01:33:11.786 --> 01:33:13.786
Yes, angry with God at God.

436
01:33:13.786 --> 01:33:15.786
But say it to Him.

437
01:33:15.786 --> 01:33:17.786
Throw it at His feet.

438
01:33:18.786 --> 01:33:22.786
And God is really not surprised by that, because He knows you much better than you know yourself.

439
01:33:23.786 --> 01:33:25.786
Do you know that...

440
01:33:26.786 --> 01:33:30.786
Psalm 139 says...

441
01:33:30.786 --> 01:33:38.786
You have already thought of me and you know me so much better than I know myself.

442
01:33:38.786 --> 01:33:43.786
Psalm 139 always gives me the peace of...

443
01:33:44.786 --> 01:33:48.786
If I do something crazy, if I do something unexpected, God knew it long ago.

444
01:33:50.786 --> 01:33:52.786
He is not surprised by it.

445
01:33:52.786 --> 01:33:54.786
He is not shocked by it.

446
01:33:54.786 --> 01:33:56.786
He does not get angry back.

447
01:33:58.786 --> 01:34:06.786
Yes, I want to pause here as a guide for a moment about the concept...

448
01:34:07.786 --> 01:34:13.786
that many reactions and expressions in life...

449
01:34:15.786 --> 01:34:19.786
You understand it as a church, as people around each other.

450
01:34:19.786 --> 01:34:21.786
And sometimes you do not understand it.

451
01:34:22.786 --> 01:34:28.786
But there is one thing you must understand as Bram.

452
01:34:28.786 --> 01:34:31.786
It is about the Lord is a shepherd.

453
01:34:31.786 --> 01:34:33.786
He is a good shepherd.

454
01:34:33.786 --> 01:34:37.786
That means a shepherd has sheep and a sheep is a flock.

455
01:34:37.786 --> 01:34:41.786
And it is of great importance that this flock stays together.

456
01:34:41.786 --> 01:34:45.786
And that this flock, that these sheep know who the shepherd is.

457
01:34:45.786 --> 01:34:48.786
So that you can go to the shepherd with your pain.

458
01:34:48.786 --> 01:34:52.786
So that when the shepherd guides you, you can follow the shepherd.

459
01:34:52.786 --> 01:34:55.786
There is one thing that is very dangerous.

460
01:34:55.786 --> 01:34:58.786
And that is isolating yourself from that flock.

461
01:34:58.786 --> 01:35:02.786
And that is what Bram was hinting at just now.

462
01:35:02.786 --> 01:35:07.786
That is when you withdraw into yourself in your pain.

463
01:35:07.786 --> 01:35:11.786
And I just prayed about that at a quarter to ten during the prayer.

464
01:35:11.786 --> 01:35:16.786
When you withdraw, of course there is a time of pain...

465
01:35:16.786 --> 01:35:22.786
And that you have no desire to open the door for someone who comes with a bouquet of flowers.

466
01:35:22.786 --> 01:35:26.786
There is time for rest and solitude, absolutely.

467
01:35:26.786 --> 01:35:30.786
Solitude is good, but there is a difference between solitude and isolation.

468
01:35:30.786 --> 01:35:34.786
Solitude is coming to rest by yourself, thinking for yourself and saying...

469
01:35:34.786 --> 01:35:36.786
Dear people, not right now.

470
01:35:36.786 --> 01:35:40.786
I want to take my time for myself and for my wife.

471
01:35:40.786 --> 01:35:44.786
Or take time for myself and God, or just for myself and for myself.

472
01:35:44.786 --> 01:35:48.786
But isolation is dangerous.

473
01:35:48.786 --> 01:35:53.786
Because within isolation, sin can be lurking.

474
01:35:53.786 --> 01:35:57.786
The Bible warns about this in various places.

475
01:35:57.786 --> 01:36:01.786
If you are angry, do not sin in your anger, says the Bible.

476
01:36:01.786 --> 01:36:03.786
How do you sin in your anger?

477
01:36:03.786 --> 01:36:08.786
By building a kind of defensive reaction, a defense mechanism...

478
01:36:09.786 --> 01:36:12.786
in your anger, perhaps even against God.

479
01:36:12.786 --> 01:36:14.786
That you say, this is not fair.

480
01:36:14.786 --> 01:36:20.786
And because it is not fair, I will not take too much notice of that whole situation of...

481
01:36:20.786 --> 01:36:23.786
do this, do not do that, what you hear from the Bible.

482
01:36:23.786 --> 01:36:27.786
And so you apply isolation from your anger.

483
01:36:27.786 --> 01:36:32.786
And you say, I will apply medication in the form of...

484
01:36:32.786 --> 01:36:37.786
and then all those isolations, dark rooms I sometimes call them, come into your heart.

485
01:36:37.786 --> 01:36:42.786
Like isolating yourself and doing things that you know are actually...

486
01:36:42.786 --> 01:36:46.786
because we all know this, that it actually has no added value...

487
01:36:46.786 --> 01:36:52.786
but they are temporary, short self-medications.

488
01:36:52.786 --> 01:36:59.786
And this is what I wanted to say, even though I can understand well that you do it...

489
01:36:59.786 --> 01:37:01.786
sin remains sin.

490
01:37:01.786 --> 01:37:03.786
And that is important.

491
01:37:03.786 --> 01:37:10.786
So suppose I know people who go through this and they fall back on drug use, for example.

492
01:37:10.786 --> 01:37:12.786
Just to name something.

493
01:37:12.786 --> 01:37:13.786
Or alcohol.

494
01:37:13.786 --> 01:37:15.786
Or pornography.

495
01:37:15.786 --> 01:37:24.786
Or any expression of an excess in life that you know is actually very bad for your life...

496
01:37:24.786 --> 01:37:29.786
but let me be because I am in pain and I do this now to ease this pain at that moment.

497
01:37:30.786 --> 01:37:39.786
Even though you understand well that this happens and you should not look judgmentally at that behavior...

498
01:37:39.786 --> 01:37:46.786
even so, the advice remains, do not do that because it does not heal.

499
01:37:46.786 --> 01:37:50.786
There is only one healer and his name is Jesus.

500
01:37:50.786 --> 01:37:56.786
So with that pain, and that is what Bram said, you still go to Jesus.

501
01:37:56.786 --> 01:37:59.786
If you are angry, go to Jesus anyway.

502
01:37:59.786 --> 01:38:04.786
If you feel the temptation of isolation rising, go to Jesus anyway.

503
01:38:04.786 --> 01:38:08.786
If you have already done it, go to Jesus again.

504
01:38:08.786 --> 01:38:13.786
Have you used drugs by now, thought about this is too much...

505
01:38:13.786 --> 01:38:17.786
suicide, used drugs, cheating, doing foolish things.

506
01:38:17.786 --> 01:38:21.786
All sins, the broad spectrum of sins that you can apply...

507
01:38:21.786 --> 01:38:24.786
that applies both to those who are grieving in their lives...

508
01:38:24.786 --> 01:38:27.786
as well as to those who have to deal with other things...

509
01:38:27.786 --> 01:38:32.786
for all sins are a result of our brokenness that is within.

510
01:38:32.786 --> 01:38:35.786
We all deal with self-medication.

511
01:38:35.786 --> 01:38:39.786
Whether you are in the pain of grief, or in another way...

512
01:38:39.786 --> 01:38:42.786
everyone commits sins for a reason.

513
01:38:42.786 --> 01:38:46.786
And yet Bram says, take it to God.

514
01:38:46.786 --> 01:38:51.786
Whether you are experiencing anger now, or the core concepts that Bram wrote down for himself...

515
01:38:51.786 --> 01:38:55.786
emptiness, fill that emptiness with God.

516
01:38:55.786 --> 01:39:00.786
Sadness, let Him be your healer.

517
01:39:03.786 --> 01:39:06.786
And then you will discover something else as well.

518
01:39:06.786 --> 01:39:09.786
People react very differently.

519
01:39:09.786 --> 01:39:13.786
Probably, your own husband or wife too.

520
01:39:14.786 --> 01:39:19.786
I have written down the question, how do you deal with people's reactions?

521
01:39:22.786 --> 01:39:25.786
Well intended, often.

522
01:39:25.786 --> 01:39:30.786
What Els and I discovered is that...

523
01:39:32.786 --> 01:39:37.786
I needed the structure, I think I went back to work within two weeks.

524
01:39:37.786 --> 01:39:41.786
I had a nice job, my job wasn't very demanding at that time.

525
01:39:43.786 --> 01:39:48.786
In hindsight, I understand that I needed that structure, but at the time I couldn't put it into words at all.

526
01:39:48.786 --> 01:39:52.786
I went crazy at home, I couldn't be at home anymore.

527
01:39:52.786 --> 01:39:56.786
Els wanted to talk, I couldn't talk, I had no words.

528
01:39:56.786 --> 01:40:00.786
I couldn't put it into words. Els wanted to talk.

529
01:40:00.786 --> 01:40:05.786
And then you start to discover that you react in a very different way.

530
01:40:05.786 --> 01:40:09.786
And also on a very different timescale.

531
01:40:09.786 --> 01:40:14.786
Because I had to work then, gone. Just do my own thing.

532
01:40:14.786 --> 01:40:16.786
That didn't go well for long, you know.

533
01:40:16.786 --> 01:40:19.786
The next spring I was home for a month.

534
01:40:19.786 --> 01:40:22.786
I couldn't concentrate anymore, I wasn't working anymore.

535
01:40:22.786 --> 01:40:24.786
I had read something and I didn't know what I had read.

536
01:40:24.786 --> 01:40:27.786
You said the next spring, so a year later.

537
01:40:27.786 --> 01:40:30.786
No, half a year later.

538
01:40:30.786 --> 01:40:33.786
So different times, different processes.

539
01:40:33.786 --> 01:40:35.786
Different processes.

540
01:40:35.786 --> 01:40:37.786
Important to know.

541
01:40:37.786 --> 01:40:40.786
And you cannot prepare for that.

542
01:40:40.786 --> 01:40:42.786
Because you don't know how you will react.

543
01:40:45.786 --> 01:40:52.786
The only thing you can do then is accept that it goes as it goes.

544
01:40:52.786 --> 01:40:54.786
And give each other space.

545
01:40:56.786 --> 01:40:58.786
But that's not easy.

546
01:40:58.786 --> 01:41:00.786
I can tell you that.

547
01:41:00.786 --> 01:41:02.786
I have learned something, Bram.

548
01:41:02.786 --> 01:41:08.786
I have learned something in a piece of basic psychology that we had to learn in our training.

549
01:41:08.786 --> 01:41:16.786
That in pastoral work in the church, and every Christian tries to apply a bit of pastoral work together.

550
01:41:16.786 --> 01:41:21.786
That in pastoral work you should never say, oh, it'll be fine.

551
01:41:21.786 --> 01:41:26.786
Because that's a remark you can do very little with.

552
01:41:26.786 --> 01:41:29.786
But it is said very often.

553
01:41:29.786 --> 01:41:36.786
I don't want to create a situation of oh, how stupid people are.

554
01:41:36.786 --> 01:41:41.786
Only, let's briefly talk about people's reactions.

555
01:41:41.786 --> 01:41:50.786
To gain insight into what is helpful and what especially does not make a difference.

556
01:41:52.786 --> 01:41:54.786
I will give some examples.

557
01:41:54.786 --> 01:42:01.786
You know what, some things hurt and are still said with the best intentions.

558
01:42:02.786 --> 01:42:05.786
Oh come on, you can try again.

559
01:42:11.786 --> 01:42:13.786
Should I try to explain it?

560
01:42:16.786 --> 01:42:22.786
It has been said to me once or twice, and both times I didn't know how to react.

561
01:42:22.786 --> 01:42:26.786
And I just walked away in disbelief.

562
01:42:27.786 --> 01:42:32.786
Maybe it was for the best, because I don't know what other reaction could have come out of it.

563
01:42:35.786 --> 01:42:37.786
It has already been a year.

564
01:42:37.786 --> 01:42:39.786
It's getting better now, right?

565
01:42:42.786 --> 01:42:43.786
Help.

566
01:42:44.786 --> 01:42:48.786
First of all, the suggestion, there is only one possible answer.

567
01:42:48.786 --> 01:42:50.786
Yes, no, it's fine like this.

568
01:42:51.786 --> 01:42:52.786
No.

569
01:42:55.786 --> 01:42:57.786
People apparently expect a standard pattern.

570
01:42:58.786 --> 01:43:02.786
People apparently expect that after a year life should be normal again.

571
01:43:02.786 --> 01:43:05.786
But let me tell you this, life has never returned to normal.

572
01:43:05.786 --> 01:43:09.786
I have recovered, but life has never gone back to how it was before.

573
01:43:09.786 --> 01:43:11.786
Because that is what people actually think or expect.

574
01:43:11.786 --> 01:43:12.786
Never.

575
01:43:17.786 --> 01:43:19.786
Oh, maybe it's better this way.

576
01:43:21.786 --> 01:43:24.786
Yes, that was the one I just hinted at, right?

577
01:43:24.786 --> 01:43:25.786
Yes.

578
01:43:25.786 --> 01:43:31.786
And that is indeed a very significant remark.

579
01:43:32.786 --> 01:43:37.786
Because you were dealing with a certain issue when Kirsten was still alive.

580
01:43:37.786 --> 01:43:45.786
And then you have the tendency as a human to think, maybe it's for the best.

581
01:43:45.786 --> 01:43:49.786
And yet it is important, however significant, that we discuss this.

582
01:43:49.786 --> 01:43:51.786
For it is not a good remark.

583
01:43:51.786 --> 01:43:52.786
Not at all.

584
01:43:52.786 --> 01:44:01.786
And it probably comes, perhaps even well-intentioned, that can really be the case.

585
01:44:02.786 --> 01:44:07.786
But it stems from a sense of what is the extra care, what are the concerns.

586
01:44:07.786 --> 01:44:14.786
But not seeing that every child, every person, is a unique person created by God.

587
01:44:15.786 --> 01:44:20.786
And I am so glad that we had Kirsten for those eight months.

588
01:44:34.786 --> 01:44:37.786
We got to know her as a unique little person.

589
01:44:37.786 --> 01:44:39.786
With her own things.

590
01:44:39.786 --> 01:44:44.786
She had her own toy that she responded to, in her own way, that she enjoyed.

591
01:44:44.786 --> 01:44:47.786
We simply learned to see her develop.

592
01:44:47.786 --> 01:44:51.786
We saw how she developed and how she responded to us and so on.

593
01:44:51.786 --> 01:44:54.786
Really just like a baby develops.

594
01:44:54.786 --> 01:44:56.786
And that is so precious.

595
01:45:01.786 --> 01:45:04.786
Do you know what can also be painful?

596
01:45:06.786 --> 01:45:08.786
Oh, you know now that she is in heaven.

597
01:45:10.786 --> 01:45:14.786
That is a thousand percent true.

598
01:45:14.786 --> 01:45:16.786
Absolutely.

599
01:45:19.786 --> 01:45:25.786
And besides, the absence here and now is just as harsh a reality.

600
01:45:29.786 --> 01:45:35.786
And that is, you know, sometimes it lies in the subtle tone in which something is said.

601
01:45:36.786 --> 01:45:43.786
But of course it is good to know that she is up there, that she is with Jesus.

602
01:45:43.786 --> 01:45:48.786
Not just in heaven, not just up there, with Jesus.

603
01:45:48.786 --> 01:45:51.786
And I know who that is, because I know Him.

604
01:45:52.786 --> 01:45:57.786
So, what a wonderful thought that He takes care of that now.

605
01:45:59.786 --> 01:46:02.786
But that does not change the loss here.

606
01:46:03.786 --> 01:46:05.786
That does not make the loss here any less.

607
01:46:06.786 --> 01:46:08.786
That exists alongside each other.

608
01:46:08.786 --> 01:46:14.786
Do you know what are good things to hear?

609
01:46:15.786 --> 01:46:18.786
When someone says, I don't know what to say.

610
01:46:18.786 --> 01:46:21.786
I am glad about that, because I don't know either.

611
01:46:22.786 --> 01:46:24.786
I also don't know what to say.

612
01:46:24.786 --> 01:46:29.786
I come to work, it is too bizarre for words that life just goes on normally.

613
01:46:30.786 --> 01:46:32.786
That is incomprehensible.

614
01:46:32.786 --> 01:46:36.786
You know, at that moment I would have liked to have a mourning band, but that no longer existed in our time.

615
01:46:36.786 --> 01:46:41.786
But you would like to express that everything is different.

616
01:46:41.786 --> 01:46:45.786
Do you understand that? The whole world looks normal again and that cannot be.

617
01:46:49.786 --> 01:46:54.786
A truly interested person, how are you, is also a good response.

618
01:46:54.786 --> 01:46:56.786
And then it doesn't matter how or what.

619
01:46:56.786 --> 01:47:00.786
And then it doesn't matter if I can only stutter that I don't know so well about it.

620
01:47:00.786 --> 01:47:02.786
That is also good.

621
01:47:03.786 --> 01:47:06.786
So even if someone says, how are you doing?

622
01:47:06.786 --> 01:47:10.786
And if no decent answer comes out, then try not to give advice anyway

623
01:47:10.786 --> 01:47:15.786
to fill in the answer that is not a complete answer.

624
01:47:15.786 --> 01:47:29.786
So I find it very important to, okay, a few years ago, it seems off topic, but it is not.

625
01:47:29.786 --> 01:47:39.786
A few years ago, when I lived in Sydney in 2008 or 2009, I once had a question for my training

626
01:47:40.786 --> 01:47:45.786
someone had a question for the professor.

627
01:47:45.786 --> 01:47:52.786
And the professor simply said, I actually don't know the answer to that.

628
01:47:52.786 --> 01:47:57.786
And that was really mind-blowing for me.

629
01:47:57.786 --> 01:48:07.786
That a Christian of that caliber, who has studied and learned Scripture and has life experience

630
01:48:07.786 --> 01:48:12.786
that a Christian can also say, I don't know the answer to this.

631
01:48:12.786 --> 01:48:15.786
That is super nice.

632
01:48:15.786 --> 01:48:21.786
Because Christians are not be-all and know-all people.

633
01:48:21.786 --> 01:48:28.786
Because then you position yourself as omniscient.

634
01:48:28.786 --> 01:48:34.786
Then you position yourself as someone who knows everything and has an answer for everything.

635
01:48:34.786 --> 01:48:39.786
But there are sometimes no answers to difficult questions.

636
01:48:39.786 --> 01:48:42.786
Sometimes they just don't exist.

637
01:48:42.786 --> 01:48:53.786
There is hope and there is also faith, but hope and faith often rise above rational thoughts.

638
01:48:53.786 --> 01:48:55.786
That is faith.

639
01:48:55.786 --> 01:49:01.786
Faith is having hope and having certainty about the things we do not see.

640
01:49:01.786 --> 01:49:07.786
And not seeing also means not being able to articulate, not seeing, not understanding.

641
01:49:07.786 --> 01:49:14.786
So as a church, and I always try to position myself this way when I deal with people in suffering.

642
01:49:14.786 --> 01:49:19.786
And also when that question is thrown at me, but why then Tim?

643
01:49:19.786 --> 01:49:28.786
I have experienced a piece of peace and a piece of reassurance that I can now say to people in this stage of life,

644
01:49:28.786 --> 01:49:31.786
I don't know, I just don't know.

645
01:49:31.786 --> 01:49:35.786
But then we don't know together and that's also not nice.

646
01:49:35.786 --> 01:49:38.786
Then we go to Jesus together.

647
01:49:38.786 --> 01:49:40.786
Right?

648
01:49:40.786 --> 01:49:49.786
So, church, you don't always have to have an opinion about everything and nothing.

649
01:49:49.786 --> 01:49:52.786
I was just talking about this with someone before the service.

650
01:49:52.786 --> 01:49:55.786
You don't always have to provide an answer.

651
01:49:55.786 --> 01:50:03.786
You also don't have to have an opinion about someone who is grieving and displaying behavior that you think shouldn't have happened.

652
01:50:03.786 --> 01:50:08.786
Please, leave judgment to Jesus.

653
01:50:08.786 --> 01:50:10.786
Give it to Him.

654
01:50:10.786 --> 01:50:14.786
And if you see someone displaying behavior that you think is sin.

655
01:50:14.786 --> 01:50:19.786
Then do this for that person, instead of feeling the need to have an opinion about it.

656
01:50:20.786 --> 01:50:28.786
Jesus says, God even says, leave vengeance to me.

657
01:50:28.786 --> 01:50:30.786
Leave healing to me.

658
01:50:30.786 --> 01:50:33.786
He is the only one who can, by the way.

659
01:50:33.786 --> 01:50:39.786
So your opinion matters very little sometimes when it comes to, I think you should do this and that now.

660
01:50:39.786 --> 01:50:47.786
First of all, you probably haven't experienced what the person in question has to go through at that moment.

661
01:50:47.786 --> 01:50:53.786
And when you experience it, it is of great value, Bram, from what you just said.

662
01:50:53.786 --> 01:50:58.786
Your wife Els went through it completely differently than how you went through it yourself.

663
01:51:00.786 --> 01:51:03.786
So, reactions from people.

664
01:51:03.786 --> 01:51:05.786
Have you had struggles in the marriage?

665
01:51:06.786 --> 01:51:08.786
About that?

666
01:51:10.786 --> 01:51:13.786
I don't know what struggle in marriage is.

667
01:51:13.786 --> 01:51:20.786
We have had quite a bit of trouble understanding each other.

668
01:51:20.786 --> 01:51:28.786
That you lose the conversation on that subject.

669
01:51:28.786 --> 01:51:34.786
Because it just doesn't work to communicate about it.

670
01:51:34.786 --> 01:51:40.786
And Els reacted to the pain in a completely different way than I did.

671
01:51:41.786 --> 01:51:46.786
And the misunderstanding of each other has had quite a significant impact.

672
01:51:46.786 --> 01:51:52.786
I appreciate that you say this, because it is a very logical result of what happens.

673
01:51:52.786 --> 01:51:56.786
You can say that in hindsight, but when you're in it, you don't understand that either.

674
01:51:58.786 --> 01:52:00.786
It is really good that you say this.

675
01:52:01.786 --> 01:52:11.786
Because indeed, you have personal pain that is already unprecedented.

676
01:52:11.786 --> 01:52:15.786
So you have personal pain that you can't deal with.

677
01:52:15.786 --> 01:52:18.786
You have personal pain and unanswered questions.

678
01:52:18.786 --> 01:52:22.786
You have personal emptiness, sadness, the list you just wrote down.

679
01:52:22.786 --> 01:52:25.786
Emptiness, sadness, it can also be anger.

680
01:52:26.786 --> 01:52:33.786
And then you also have to deal in that marriage with someone who also has a list.

681
01:52:33.786 --> 01:52:38.786
And also exhibits behavior that is not beautiful.

682
01:52:40.786 --> 01:52:45.786
And then you have to deal with your pain along with a second person in pain.

683
01:52:45.786 --> 01:52:48.786
Then you can't really handle it at all, actually.

684
01:52:48.786 --> 01:52:51.786
At least, then you get that misunderstanding.

685
01:52:52.786 --> 01:52:56.786
Yes, fortunately that has not led to major problems for us.

686
01:52:56.786 --> 01:53:01.786
But that is despite ourselves, I think.

687
01:53:01.786 --> 01:53:04.786
Yes, we will still go for it.

688
01:53:06.786 --> 01:53:08.786
Okay, I have one last question.

689
01:53:10.786 --> 01:53:15.786
And this is the important question. How do you deal with healing and processing?

690
01:53:16.786 --> 01:53:20.786
A classic question, Bram.

691
01:53:20.786 --> 01:53:24.786
Have you processed it yet? Are you healed yet?

692
01:53:24.786 --> 01:53:29.786
What a great question. Most of the time I don't know what that means.

693
01:53:29.786 --> 01:53:33.786
Most people who ask the question, have you processed it yet, think...

694
01:53:33.786 --> 01:53:37.786
If the answer is yes, then everything is back to how it used to be.

695
01:53:37.786 --> 01:53:41.786
And then it will never be. It will really never be.

696
01:53:41.786 --> 01:53:46.786
So if that is the intention of the question, then I say, I will never process it.

697
01:53:46.786 --> 01:53:49.786
Only, that is also not true.

698
01:53:49.786 --> 01:53:53.786
Because there is a form of recovery.

699
01:53:57.786 --> 01:54:00.786
It is also not true that time holds all wonders.

700
01:54:03.786 --> 01:54:08.786
If it is only the effect of time, then...

701
01:54:08.786 --> 01:54:10.786
No, I do not believe so.

702
01:54:10.786 --> 01:54:17.786
It is true that at a certain point you start doing the daily things again.

703
01:54:17.786 --> 01:54:24.786
And eventually life returns to its normal...

704
01:54:24.786 --> 01:54:27.786
Life moves forward again.

705
01:54:28.786 --> 01:54:31.786
At first, that is a bizarre experience.

706
01:54:31.786 --> 01:54:37.786
But over time, you have your daily life with God.

707
01:54:37.786 --> 01:54:41.786
You have your life in the congregation, you have the family that functions, that continues.

708
01:54:41.786 --> 01:54:46.786
You also must not forget the one-and-a-half-year-old daughter.

709
01:54:46.786 --> 01:54:51.786
Our son Stefan was born shortly, a few years later.

710
01:54:53.786 --> 01:54:56.786
Life takes on its shape again.

711
01:54:57.786 --> 01:55:00.786
And recovery has gone very differently for Els.

712
01:55:00.786 --> 01:55:02.786
Els really has her own story about that.

713
01:55:02.786 --> 01:55:06.786
Which has very different aspects than what I have experienced.

714
01:55:07.786 --> 01:55:11.786
One thing has been a very recognizable moment for me.

715
01:55:11.786 --> 01:55:15.786
Because recovery happens in small things that you sometimes do not even recognize.

716
01:55:15.786 --> 01:55:20.786
And sometimes it happens in things where you suddenly realize, something special is happening here.

717
01:55:22.786 --> 01:55:25.786
Memory is a strange thing.

718
01:55:29.786 --> 01:55:35.786
It must have been about six or seven years after Kirsten's passing.

719
01:55:36.786 --> 01:55:38.786
And I was active in the church.

720
01:55:38.786 --> 01:55:42.786
And I ended up at a Saturday morning meeting for leaders.

721
01:55:42.786 --> 01:55:44.786
And people were prayed for.

722
01:55:44.786 --> 01:55:47.786
Do you hear this? Six, seven years later.

723
01:55:47.786 --> 01:55:51.786
So let's gain some insight into time and periods.

724
01:55:55.786 --> 01:55:59.786
It wasn't a specific prayer for this subject at all.

725
01:55:59.786 --> 01:56:03.786
I wasn't intensely focused on it at that moment.

726
01:56:04.786 --> 01:56:06.786
But God knew what was needed.

727
01:56:06.786 --> 01:56:09.786
And there was just prayer, Holy Spirit.

728
01:56:09.786 --> 01:56:14.786
Just, you know, in the sense of, yes, that's how we are sometimes used to praying.

729
01:56:14.786 --> 01:56:16.786
Holy Spirit, do what is needed.

730
01:56:16.786 --> 01:56:18.786
That is the open attitude towards God.

731
01:56:18.786 --> 01:56:23.786
That is an open attitude of, here I am, I make myself available.

732
01:56:23.786 --> 01:56:25.786
Go ahead.

733
01:56:33.786 --> 01:56:46.786
That time, God brought back all sorts of memories that I was no longer consciously aware of.

734
01:56:48.786 --> 01:56:58.786
Memories of how it felt to have Kirsten on my shoulder.

735
01:56:59.786 --> 01:57:01.786
What her little smile was like.

736
01:57:04.786 --> 01:57:09.786
How she, I had a little mustache at that time.

737
01:57:09.786 --> 01:57:12.786
That's the funny thing when you're young.

738
01:57:12.786 --> 01:57:14.786
Yes, indeed.

739
01:57:14.786 --> 01:57:18.786
How she always wanted to grab my mustache.

740
01:57:18.786 --> 01:57:21.786


741
01:57:21.786 --> 01:57:27.786
And you know, that young babies can have those fine sharp little nails.

742
01:57:27.786 --> 01:57:30.786
That is the punishment for that mustache.

743
01:57:30.786 --> 01:57:32.786
Yes, that must be it.

744
01:57:33.786 --> 01:57:43.786
But you know that, right after the passing, there are memories, the things you still have.

745
01:57:47.786 --> 01:57:55.786
And that is, I had a few hours where I couldn't keep my eyes dry anymore.

746
01:57:55.786 --> 01:57:58.786
I cried so much then.

747
01:57:58.786 --> 01:57:59.786
Yes.

748
01:58:01.786 --> 01:58:11.786
All those, I can't even name them all now, but so many of the daily memories that I was no longer consciously aware of.

749
01:58:11.786 --> 01:58:15.786
And that has done so incredibly well.

750
01:58:17.786 --> 01:58:21.786
That has brought so much peace.

751
01:58:23.786 --> 01:58:25.786
In so many ways.

752
01:58:26.786 --> 01:58:32.786
I wish I had the words now to truly describe the depth of what happened, but I don't have them.

753
01:58:32.786 --> 01:58:34.786
I think it does come through.

754
01:58:36.786 --> 01:58:48.786
But, Bram, can you imagine that six, seven, or eight years later you experience something very intensive?

755
01:58:48.786 --> 01:58:53.786
What feels healing at that moment.

756
01:58:53.786 --> 01:59:00.786
Can you imagine that, for example, in year twelve you could still go through an enormous deep valley?

757
01:59:00.786 --> 01:59:04.786
Would that be possible? Would that not be possible? Could that happen?

758
01:59:05.786 --> 01:59:07.786
I think everything is possible with faithfulness and sorrow.

759
01:59:07.786 --> 01:59:08.786
Yes.

760
01:59:08.786 --> 01:59:15.786
There are still, even now, moments when I suddenly get touched and memories come up.

761
01:59:15.786 --> 01:59:18.786
And I am just a bit out of the world.

762
01:59:18.786 --> 01:59:23.786
Please don't address me for a moment, then I can't do anything, then I won't say anything, then I am just...

763
01:59:23.786 --> 01:59:28.786
It can just be about an everyday thing, it can be about a movie where suddenly something comes up.

764
01:59:28.786 --> 01:59:29.786
Yes, of course.

765
01:59:29.786 --> 01:59:31.786
That can be about...

766
01:59:32.786 --> 01:59:34.786
About a piece of reflection.

767
01:59:34.786 --> 01:59:43.786
Well, I find it important to ask this question because, indeed, in those reactions we just talked about,

768
01:59:43.786 --> 01:59:49.786
people can say, okay, it's been a year now, how do you stand now? Is it finished now?

769
01:59:49.786 --> 01:59:51.786
You know, bizarre, but it is so.

770
01:59:52.786 --> 01:59:56.786
That we go through that thought pattern, but yes, how long then?

771
01:59:56.786 --> 02:00:00.786
Two years? Six years? Eight years? Twelve years?

772
02:00:00.786 --> 02:00:07.786
And could it be that in year six you experience something wonderful, together with God, and that in year twelve you go through hell?

773
02:00:07.786 --> 02:00:09.786
That is quite possible.

774
02:00:09.786 --> 02:00:20.786
Let me inform us, it is quite possible that people go through various situations for the rest of their lives.

775
02:00:20.786 --> 02:00:26.786
So in year thirty you can still have to go through pain and sorrow,

776
02:00:26.786 --> 02:00:31.786
for something that you experience in year ten, as a piece of healing, at that moment.

777
02:00:31.786 --> 02:00:41.786
And I have talked about this more often with the congregation, and it doesn't always elicit the best reactions in the church.

778
02:00:41.786 --> 02:00:48.786
But I believe one hundred percent in healing. One hundred percent.

779
02:00:48.786 --> 02:00:55.786
And yet I know that some things mark us for the rest of our earthly lives.

780
02:00:56.786 --> 02:01:01.786
Yes, but Tim, didn't you say that we are changed through Jesus?

781
02:01:01.786 --> 02:01:07.786
I know, but that doesn't mean that membership marks can't still be there.

782
02:01:07.786 --> 02:01:10.786
That sometimes go hand in hand with pain.

783
02:01:10.786 --> 02:01:12.786
For life.

784
02:01:12.786 --> 02:01:21.786
Because, you can say that to me, like yes but Tim, we have to go through the cross completely finished,

785
02:01:21.786 --> 02:01:24.786
be perfect and stand in our healing.

786
02:01:24.786 --> 02:01:31.786
And if you don't do that at that moment, then you stand there, or you don't go through it properly.

787
02:01:31.786 --> 02:01:36.786
But I can, let me put it this way, with my human mind, I can't match that.

788
02:01:36.786 --> 02:01:41.786
If I believe in Jesus, I can still have pain.

789
02:01:41.786 --> 02:01:44.786
And that's how I just deal with it.

790
02:01:44.786 --> 02:01:49.786
And I also see it happening in people who...

791
02:01:49.786 --> 02:01:51.786
I have a lot of respect for you Bram.

792
02:01:51.786 --> 02:01:53.786
And I look up to you immensely.

793
02:01:53.786 --> 02:01:58.786
And you are together with Els elder of this church.

794
02:01:58.786 --> 02:02:01.786
And I see faith in you.

795
02:02:01.786 --> 02:02:06.786
And at the same time you speak together through the situations,

796
02:02:06.786 --> 02:02:11.786
that you can go through different phases of healing.

797
02:02:11.786 --> 02:02:18.786
And then again, it seems like, you know the concept three steps forward, two steps back, you know that concept right?

798
02:02:20.786 --> 02:02:26.786
Do we believe that we can also take this walk three steps forward, two steps back, together with Jesus?

799
02:02:26.786 --> 02:02:28.786
That's an important question.

800
02:02:28.786 --> 02:02:36.786
Do we allow it, that it's three steps forward, two steps back, together with Jesus, that that is possible?

801
02:02:36.786 --> 02:02:38.786
I think so.

802
02:02:38.786 --> 02:02:40.786
Yes, I think so.

803
02:02:41.786 --> 02:02:46.786
Because otherwise it has to be just three steps forward, three steps forward, three steps forward.

804
02:02:46.786 --> 02:02:50.786
I just don't see it happening, let me put it that way. I just don't see that.

805
02:02:50.786 --> 02:02:56.786
You know, Christ restores now and here. Christ heals now and here, absolutely.

806
02:02:56.786 --> 02:02:58.786
But perfection is yet to come.

807
02:02:58.786 --> 02:03:00.786
We do not have perfection here yet.

808
02:03:02.786 --> 02:03:05.786
I think that covers most of it.

809
02:03:05.786 --> 02:03:08.786
But I also want to testify about that.

810
02:03:08.786 --> 02:03:12.786
We just sang the song, It is well with my soul.

811
02:03:12.786 --> 02:03:16.786
And that touched me so much, because that's how it is.

812
02:03:16.786 --> 02:03:20.786
I can say, it is well with my soul.

813
02:03:20.786 --> 02:03:22.786
Yes, there is a scar on it.

814
02:03:22.786 --> 02:03:27.786
Yes, it happens that all sorts of things touch me.

815
02:03:27.786 --> 02:03:30.786
But you know, I wouldn't want it any other way.

816
02:03:30.786 --> 02:03:35.786
Because that would mean that Kirsten's life was not very important.

817
02:03:36.786 --> 02:03:43.786
It cannot be that something like that happens and then you can just go on as if nothing is wrong.

818
02:03:43.786 --> 02:03:45.786
That is impossible, that is inconceivable.

819
02:03:45.786 --> 02:03:47.786
Could you repeat that one more time, please?

820
02:03:47.786 --> 02:03:52.786
That is very significant what you just said, but still important.

821
02:03:52.786 --> 02:03:55.786
So would you like to repeat that once more?

822
02:03:55.786 --> 02:04:07.786
If you could really go on as if nothing happened, how important has it been then?

823
02:04:07.786 --> 02:04:11.786
How much influence has it had?

824
02:04:15.786 --> 02:04:22.786
I would not, if there were no visible, noticeable, and tangible traces now,

825
02:04:23.786 --> 02:04:26.786
then I would regret it.

826
02:04:34.786 --> 02:04:40.786
I have experienced a tremendous amount of healing, but it is part of me that this has happened.

827
02:04:40.786 --> 02:04:43.786
It is part of my life that this has happened.

828
02:04:43.786 --> 02:04:47.786
It is part of who I am that this has happened.

829
02:04:47.786 --> 02:04:50.786
And that is a reality.

830
02:04:51.786 --> 02:05:00.786
And in that, with everything, how and what, I can now say, it is well with my soul.

831
02:05:00.786 --> 02:05:03.786
Really. It is truly well.

832
02:05:03.786 --> 02:05:11.786
And yes, at the same time I can be touched by something and memories come rushing back and emotions arise.

833
02:05:11.786 --> 02:05:13.786
But that is also good.

834
02:05:14.786 --> 02:05:16.786
That has its place in life.

835
02:05:16.786 --> 02:05:20.786
We are immensely grateful that we could care for Kirsten.

836
02:05:20.786 --> 02:05:25.786
We are immensely grateful for everything we experienced with her.

837
02:05:25.786 --> 02:05:28.786
We gave what we could.

838
02:05:28.786 --> 02:05:31.786
It has gone as it has gone.

839
02:05:31.786 --> 02:05:34.786
With God we have a beautiful life now.

840
02:05:34.786 --> 02:05:37.786
Shall we leave it at that?

841
02:05:37.786 --> 02:05:39.786
Shall we stand, people?

842
02:05:39.786 --> 02:05:43.786
Can we honor Bram with a round of applause?

843
02:05:43.786 --> 02:05:45.786
A round of applause.

844
02:05:50.786 --> 02:05:52.786
Wait a moment, wait a moment.

845
02:06:08.786 --> 02:06:12.786
Shall we close our eyes? Bram is going to pray for us.

846
02:06:13.786 --> 02:06:17.786
Yes, let the cadet guide himself.

847
02:06:19.786 --> 02:06:25.786
Heavenly Father, you are the God who is always there.

848
02:06:26.786 --> 02:06:32.786
You are the God who knows everyone and knows them personally.

849
02:06:33.786 --> 02:06:38.786
You are the only good, true Father and good Lord.

850
02:06:39.786 --> 02:06:46.786
I want to pray now for people who are struggling in sorrow.

851
02:06:47.786 --> 02:06:50.786
People who are struggling with loss.

852
02:06:52.786 --> 02:06:58.786
Father, I pray that you reach out to people in their inner being, in their souls.

853
02:06:58.786 --> 02:07:01.786
Your Holy Spirit works in restoration.

854
02:07:02.786 --> 02:07:05.786
That can be in so many ways.

855
02:07:05.786 --> 02:07:11.786
It doesn't matter what the loss is. It doesn't matter what the grief is.

856
02:07:11.786 --> 02:07:15.786
But you are a God who knows.

857
02:07:15.786 --> 02:07:18.786
You are the God who understands.

858
02:07:18.786 --> 02:07:22.786
You are the God who is not startled and who does not blame.

859
02:07:22.786 --> 02:07:24.786
For you bring restoration.

860
02:07:24.786 --> 02:07:30.786
And so, I want to bless us all in the name of Jesus.

861
02:07:31.786 --> 02:07:35.786
For there is restoration in Jesus' name.

862
02:07:35.786 --> 02:07:37.786
Amen.

863
02:07:43.786 --> 02:07:44.786
We are going to sing this song.

864
02:07:44.786 --> 02:07:47.786
It is well with my soul. Sing it with faith.

865
02:07:49.786 --> 02:07:53.786
I close this service in the name of Jesus.

866
02:07:54.786 --> 02:07:58.786
But after this song, the service is now over.

867
02:07:58.786 --> 02:08:00.786
You can go have a cup of coffee shortly.

868
02:08:00.786 --> 02:08:02.786
And we have a good time together.

869
02:08:02.786 --> 02:08:05.786
And we have hope and joy in the name of Jesus.

870
02:08:05.786 --> 02:08:10.786
But if you feel the need to come forward after this song.

871
02:08:10.786 --> 02:08:12.786
Then we would like to pray with you.

872
02:08:12.786 --> 02:08:17.786
For this topic needs prayer continuously.

873
02:08:17.786 --> 02:08:18.786
For life.

874
02:08:18.786 --> 02:08:24.786
So I would appreciate it if some of our leaders could come forward.

875
02:08:24.786 --> 02:08:30.786
So that we can pray for each other if there is a need in Jesus' name.

876
02:08:30.786 --> 02:08:33.786
Shall we sing this song with full conviction.

877
02:08:33.786 --> 02:08:35.786
I bless us in the name of Jesus.

878
02:08:35.786 --> 02:08:37.786
Thank you for coming.

879
02:08:37.786 --> 02:08:40.786
And I hope that this service has been a blessing for your life.

880
02:08:40.786 --> 02:08:42.786
Until tomorrow.

